\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Polyimide on silicon ($d$ in \si {\micro \metre }, $\tau $ in \si {\femto \second }): best of eight starts with free $\tau $, $a$; CR bound (none for $\kappa _{\mathrm  {Si}}$, at $\kappa \ge 0$); fit without $\tau $, $a$; independent values ($^a$white light, \SI {633}{\nano \metre }; $^b$profilometer; $^c$Ref.~\cite  {Dai2004}; $^d$product of the values marked $^a$ and $^b$, a guide only). With $n_{\mathrm  {Si}}=3.4175$ fixed: $d_{\mathrm  {PI}}=25.25$, $\tau =-65.4$, rMSE $1.70\sigma $. The 2 of 8 starts within \SI {0.5}{\percent } of the best rMSE agree on $n_{\mathrm  {PI}}d_{\mathrm  {PI}}$ to \SI {0.22}{\percent }.}}{3}{table.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:pi}{{1}{3}{Polyimide on silicon ($d$ in \si {\micro \metre }, $\tau $ in \si {\femto \second }): best of eight starts with free $\tau $, $a$; CR bound (none for $\kS $, at $\kap \ge 0$); fit without $\tau $, $a$; independent values ($^a$white light, \SI {633}{\nano \metre }; $^b$profilometer; $^c$Ref.~\cite {Dai2004}; $^d$product of the values marked $^a$ and $^b$, a guide only). With $\nS =3.4175$ fixed: $d_{\mathrm {PI}}=25.25$, $\tau =-65.4$, rMSE $1.70\sigma $. The 2 of 8 starts within \SI {0.5}{\percent } of the best rMSE agree on $n_{\mathrm {PI}}d_{\mathrm {PI}}$ to \SI {0.22}{\percent }}{table.caption.2}{}}
