\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Adam in the PCA planes of its path. Grey: log loss, lighter is lower. Axes: variance fraction and composition of each component, nominal-scaled (1 = q, 2 = Si). $+$ Adam end point, $\bullet $ start, $\star $ end of phase; path numbers: iteration. (a)--(c) Phase~I (iterations 1--1615), one plane per start, axes scaled by $\sqrt  {G_{ii}}$, $G=J^\top J/L$; loss falls by 81--\SI {92}{\percent }. (d) Phase~II, shared plane, fractional coordinates (\SI {99.7}{\percent } of the variance), spanned by $\kappa _{\mathrm  q}$, $\kappa _{\mathrm  {Si}}$; loss falls by 22--\SI {29}{\percent }. (e) Loss. Singular values $s_1\ldots  s_6$ of $J/\sqrt  L$: 8.66 (total optical thickness), 1.54 (optical thickness moved between layers), 0.69 (physical thickness at fixed delay, mainly $d_{\mathrm  q}$), 0.073 (thickness transfer), 0.019 (total attenuation), 0.0016 (attenuation split).}}{5}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:twophase}{{3}{5}{Adam in the PCA planes of its path. Grey: log loss, lighter is lower. Axes: variance fraction and composition of each component, nominal-scaled (1 = q, 2 = Si). $+$ Adam end point, $\bullet $ start, $\star $ end of phase; path numbers: iteration. (a)--(c) Phase~I (iterations 1--1615), one plane per start, axes scaled by $\sqrt {G_{ii}}$, $G=J^\top J/L$; loss falls by 81--\SI {92}{\percent }. (d) Phase~II, shared plane, fractional coordinates (\SI {99.7}{\percent } of the variance), spanned by $\kq $, $\kS $; loss falls by 22--\SI {29}{\percent }. (e) Loss. Singular values $s_1\ldots s_6$ of $J/\sqrt L$: 8.66 (total optical thickness), 1.54 (optical thickness moved between layers), 0.69 (physical thickness at fixed delay, mainly $\dq $), 0.073 (thickness transfer), 0.019 (total attenuation), 0.0016 (attenuation split)}{figure.caption.5}{}}
